    "authors": [
      "rules-as-references conformance (esm-spec §9.6.3 constraint 7, §9.6.4 rule 3)"
    ],
    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.4 rule 3: the match-less template `ddx` holds a spatial `D` and is called with `u` (declared shape [x]) and `v` (declared shape [x, y]): two instances. Inside the body the parameter `f` is a leaf that a `where` shape constraint reads through its instance, so `central_1d` fires in the first and `central_2d` in the second. The two rewritten bodies differ, so they are registered as `ddx.variant1` (the reference to `central_1d`, first in canonical byte order) and `ddx.variant2`, each call site is re-pointed to its instance's variant, and `ddx` stays as authored. Both rules are referenced and materialize match-less in their authored positions. `expanded.esm` is the tree the eager-expansion engine produced.",
    "name": "template_instance_variants"
  },
